"Generalised Stretched Littlewood-Richardson Coefficients (https://arxiv.org/abs/0904.4778)\nciteturn0academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 17.5 years ago; Title: Generalised Stretched Littlewood-Richardson Coefficients ... The Littlewood-Richardson (LR) coefficient counts among many other things the LR tableaux of a given shape and a given content.\nTitle: Generalised Stretched Littlewood-Richardson Coefficients\nAuthors: Christian Gutschwager\nDate: Thu Apr 30 10:33:17 2009\n\nThe Littlewood-Richardson (LR) coefficient counts among many other things the LR tableaux of a given shape and a given content. We prove, that the number of LR tableaux weakly increases if one adds to the shape and the content the shape and the content of another LR tableau. We also investigate the behaviour of the number of LR tableaux, if one repeatedly adds to the shape another shape with either fixed or arbitrary content. This is a generalisation of the stretched LR coefficients, where one repeatedly adds the same shape and content to itself.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTHE LATTICE OF INTEGER FLOWS (https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/document?doi=f119410457c62ddfd57002a0399745ba81f7d28b&repid=rep1&type=pdf)\nciteturn0search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10 months ago; LATTICE OF INTEGER FLOWS ... matroid (M, E) represented over C by a ... matrices, and these yield Eisenstein ﬂow lattices that have bases with ... Conjecture 25. ... Let M and N be sixth-root-of-unity matroids.\nLATTICE OF INTEGER FLOWS\n17\nmatroid (M, E) represented over C by a\n6√\n1 matrix M is the lattice of\nEisenstein ﬂows\nΛE(M) = kerC(M) ∩EE.\nThe inner product on ΛE(M) is induced by the Hermitian inner product\non CE.\nSuch a lattice is not just an abelian group, but even an E-module.\nThis allows a stronger version of isometry: ψ : Λ →Λ′ is an E-isometry\nif it is a bijection such that both ψ and ψ−1 are E-module homomor-\nphisms that preserve the inner products 